# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Query correctness: questions the surface has to answer correctly.
#
# Each expectation names the target and the entity the answer must contain. A query
# that returns a superset still passes, because a walk is allowed to reach more
# than was asked for; a query that omits the named entity fails.
#
# `impl Trait for Type` binds the **impl block**, which the Rust spec maps to
# `EntityKind::Module` with the type's name. So "which types implement `Clock`"
# is answered by a walk that reaches `module | Ticks`, not `struct | Ticks`. The
# expectation names the module because that is the entity the edge reaches, and a
# reader who wanted the struct would be asking a different question.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
callers | src/service.rs | function | retry | src/service.rs | method | Runner.run
callers | src/report.rs | method | Sink.push | src/report.rs | function | render
callers | src/report.rs | function | format_line_inner | src/report.rs | function | format_line
callers | src/model.rs | function | entry | src/report.rs | function | format_line
callers | src/model.rs | function | entry | src/report.rs | function | renamed
callers | src/model.rs | function | entry | src/service.rs | function | with_clock
callees | src/service.rs | function | describe | src/service.rs | function | format_line
implementations | src/traits.rs | trait | Clock | src/traits.rs | module | Ticks
implementations | src/traits.rs | trait | Saveable | src/traits.rs | module | Meters

# `callees(summarise)` cannot reach `describe`. The call is written
# `service::describe(entry)`, whose path has one segment, and the walker marks a
# single-segment path ambiguous on purpose because `Type::method()` is
# byte-identical to it — so this edge is `unresolved` and the honest answer is a
# shorter callee list. It is in this file because the number it produces is the
# finding, not an accident of the fixture.
callees | src/lib.rs | function | summarise | src/service.rs | function | describe

